 "text": "Hey, how's your day been so far? The easiest is a cable tray, either the flat ones on top of the desk or the sloping ones on side. No problem. I' lost you there for a second. It' bit fiddly, yes. You need to measure your desk first, usually about thirty centimetres from the back wall. Then the tray goes on the desk itself, not the wall, so it doesn't have to reach. For laptop and few cords, a small tray is plenty.",
